  "body": "v16.43 proves the complete exact-fiber classification for rooted stars with m,k>=2 and any feasible hitting number q.\n\nEvery exact-q fiber is connected unless m=k=q. In that fully packed exception there are m! isolated states, and the three independent scalar barriers between distinct states are 1; the separately named LEX triple is (1,1,1). Connected fibers have barrier 0. The proof contracts supports onto a minimum hitting set, then uses either a spare leaf or a spare label to reach a canonical singleton coloring. This is a theorem about stars; nested branching interactions and universal unit barriers remain unresolved.\n\nProspective finite scope: all (m,k) in {2,3,4}\u00d7{2,3,4}, plus (5,2),(5,3), all admitted states, primitive edges and attained profiles. Production and independent verification reconstruct the complete identities. The copied v16.41 graph engines explicitly restrict the fully packed classification to k equal to the leaf count; q=m alone is insufficient with spare labels.\n\nObserved: STAR_CLASSIFICATION_VALIDATED. All 74,185 state-normalization certificates across 28 profiles passed. No classification failure, construction failure or nonunit pair. The nontrivial component pairs are the 292 fully packed pairs; 25 other profiles are exact-connected. Per-graph component counts aggregate across profiles, not within one fiber. Prior small-star threshold evidence is disclosed in preregistration; the general proof and full normalization campaign are prospective, not a claimed blinded replication.\n\nVerified parent: 4c8df6179496d8a5a6304443e4a5c7ade6a4ff6f.\nProspective protocol: f656f5ee61f970746aec1e3b8f1b854694bac0be (direct parent link checked).\nScientific source: 1c73d9aaa74e85e2a6a35f302963d86e1f2688d1.\nScientific run: https://github.com/proteinfoldingengine/WetLabEngine/actions/runs/36797815686\n\nThe first execution passed all 431 inherited + 44 new = 475 checks, two expected-failure diagnostics, fresh v16.42/nested parent replay, and independent full graph/path verification. Root audit checked API ZIP digest, all 54 manifest files, all 1,425 source/input Git blobs, complete passing test logs and byte-identical parent science. Independent mathematical/source review preceded execution, and independent result review confirmed the interpretation.\n\nPublication commit: 1d07d5ebe233904ac841bab01797d2858a94126b. Fresh reproduction passed all 475 checks and reproduced every scientific byte. Root independently verified all 134 publication-manifest entries and Git blobs; the sole publication commit adds generated evidence and does not alter scientific source.\n\nTransport audit: the first local publication download was truncated (65,306,624 bytes) and rejected by its hash check. A fresh download has the API-recorded 66,625,028 bytes and SHA256 be9b0f55fd87ee249a230f0581067fc109dcdd748536b426fb612dc1d1e8d543; complete ZIP, manifest, source and reproduction audits then passed. No scientific rerun or source modification was needed.\n\nStatus: READY FOR MERGE; actual-merge replay and verified durable receipt still required.",
